1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:04,919
So how did two best friends go from this You're always like this when you're worried.

2
00:00:05,839 --> 00:00:06,259
Like what?

3
00:00:06,799 --> 00:00:11,179
Disagreeable. To this No, stay with the king!

4
00:00:11,259 --> 00:00:12,050
Hold your friends!

5
00:00:13,009 --> 00:00:15,759
Then again, this show is in the Game of Thrones universe,

6
00:00:16,719 --> 00:00:19,160
so friends trying to kill each other is just an average Tuesday.

7
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,079
That's right, we're talking about House of the Dragon,

8
00:00:22,339 --> 00:00:26,019
the ongoing prequel show to one of the greatest fantasy shows of all time.

9
00:00:26,519 --> 00:00:30,480
Bum-ba-ba-da-bum-ba-ba-da-bum-ba-da-bum-ba-da-bum-bum-ba-da-ba-ba-ba-ba-ba!

10
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:31,460
Man, I love that theme.

11
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:36,640
Before I begin, I highly recommend you watch our video on Game of Thrones first before watching this video,

12
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:39,060
so I'm going to be skipping over some stuff that I've already established.

13
00:00:39,539 --> 00:00:44,240
Roughly a century before the events of the show, the Targaryens, led by Aegon the Conqueror,

14
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:46,200
conquered the continent of Westeros.

15
00:00:46,759 --> 00:00:51,399
Aegon was able to achieve this due to the help of his sister wives, Visenya and Rhaenys,

16
00:00:51,579 --> 00:00:53,859
as well as their three big-ass dragons.

17
00:00:54,219 --> 00:00:59,359
They burned his enemies and created treaties with the other houses such as House Stark and House Lannister.

18
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,420
Aegon established his rule over Westeros in King's Landing,

19
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:07,400
upon the heavily coveted Iron Throne which was forged from the blades of his surrendered enemies.

20
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:08,900
So freaking cool.

21
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:13,859
When Aegon died, the line of succession passed to his son and future Targaryen children,

22
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:18,959
and over time, Targaryens continued to ride dragons and established their rule over Westeros.

23
00:01:19,099 --> 00:01:23,680
They also developed a susceptibility for growing mad the more they tried to maintain their rule,

24
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,260
as well as marrying within the family so that their lineage would remain, uh, pure.

25
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:33,840
100 years later, and 200 years before the events of Game of Thrones, King Jaehaerys Targaryen,

26
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:34,980
known as the Old King,

27
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:40,640
named his grandson Viserys Targaryen the successor to the Iron Throne and the King of Westeros.

28
00:01:40,959 --> 00:01:46,459
This was controversial because Viserys' older sister, Rhaenys Targaryen, was theoretically promised the throne.

29
00:01:46,739 --> 00:01:48,019
Yeah, there's drama already.

30
00:01:48,239 --> 00:01:53,640
Jaehaerys gave the succession to Viserys only because Rhaenys was a woman, despite having a stronger claim.

31
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:58,379
This really upset Rhaenys' husband, Lord Corlys Velaryon of House Velaryon,

32
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:02,200
as he wanted nothing more than to see his wife and his house ascend to the Iron Throne.

33
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:07,140
House Velaryon never rode dragons, but made a name for themselves by becoming shipmasters and seamen,

34
00:02:07,439 --> 00:02:09,560
hence why Corlys' nickname is the Sea Snake.

35
00:02:09,939 --> 00:02:15,159
Viserys' wife, Emma Arryn, was already pregnant when Jaehaerys named Viserys as his successor,

36
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:17,319
assuming she would give birth to a healthy boy.

37
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:21,729
Unfortunately, she gave birth to a healthy girl, Rhaenyra Targaryen.

38
00:02:22,159 --> 00:02:24,699
So things are not looking good for Viserys and House Targaryen.

39
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:28,800
When Rhaenyra was born, Viserys and Rhaenyra's relationship became very distant,

40
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:31,409
to the point that he hardly acknowledges her as his firstborn.

41
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:33,060
Father of the year, am I right?

42
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:37,819
This made Rhaenyra become closer to Viserys' rebellious younger brother, Daemon Targaryen.

43
00:02:38,159 --> 00:02:41,419
For a long time, people considered having Daemon be Viserys' successor.

44
00:02:41,699 --> 00:02:44,960
But Daemon didn't have a clear path to succession, which made Daemon very upset,

45
00:02:45,199 --> 00:02:48,520
and he began doing everything in his power to prove that he was worthy of being king.

46
00:02:48,919 --> 00:02:50,860
This may explain why he's grown so close to Rhaenyra.

47
00:02:51,259 --> 00:02:55,340
Because if he marries his niece, the path to the throne will be a lot easier for him.

48
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:59,139
Okay. And that is the basic context of the show.

49
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:02,139
I'll go into more storylines and introduce more characters as we go along.

50
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:05,740
So without further ado, let us once again attempt to play the Game of Thrones,

51
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:13,319
or in this case, dance the Dance of Dragons, as we uncover the story that is House of the Dragon.

52
00:03:14,039 --> 00:03:19,259
The show begins in the ninth year of Viserys' reign, where we see a young Princess Rhaenyra riding her dragon,

53
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:22,460
Cyrax, over King's Landing like the carefree princess that she is.

54
00:03:22,819 --> 00:03:27,379
She lands in the Dragonpit, which is the stable for the dragons and is greeted by Sir Harold Westerling,

55
00:03:27,979 --> 00:03:32,199
the commander of the Kingsguard, and her best friend, Alicent Hightower of House Hightower.

56
00:03:32,719 --> 00:03:37,620
To say Rhaenyra and Alicent are best friends is an understatement, as these two have been inseparable since birth.

57
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:41,400
One could argue there is an affectionate romance blossoming between the two.

58
00:03:41,719 --> 00:03:47,139
Alicent is also the daughter of Sir Otto Hightower, who is currently serving as the Hand of the King,

59
00:03:47,379 --> 00:03:50,379
and secretly wants nothing more than to see his house on the Iron Throne.

60
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:54,400
At this time, Rhaenyra's mother, Emma, is once again pregnant with Viserys' child,

61
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:57,919
and many believe it will be a boy, finally giving Viserys an heir.

62
00:03:58,349 --> 00:04:02,139
Viserys is so certain that he will have a son that he's holding a tournament to honor his birth,

63
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:04,520
and is inviting everybody all over Westeros to attend.

64
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:09,159
Unfortunately, Emma has been sick lately, so there's been a lot of stress over her surviving the labor,

65
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:12,400
let alone giving birth to a healthy son after so many miscarriages lately.

66
00:04:18,410 --> 00:04:20,319
While Viserys plans for the birth of his son,

67
00:04:20,519 --> 00:04:25,019
Daemon flaunts his power by brutally rounding up all the criminals in King's Landing using the City Watch.

68
00:04:25,439 --> 00:04:30,579
This makes the Targaryens look very bad, so Viserys holds a small council meeting to determine Daemon's actions.

69
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:37,199
Otto strongly rebukes what Daemon did, but Corlys, also on the council as the master of ships, defends Daemon's actions.

70
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:42,579
Corlys argues that Daemon took extreme measures to ensure the safety of all of Westeros' nobility for the tournament,

71
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:49,480
but it's clear Corlys is only defending Daemon because they both know that Otto has been secretly trying to gain favor with Viserys for years.

72
00:04:49,839 --> 00:04:55,680
The conversation shifts to a personal attack on Daemon's estranged relationship to his wife, Lady Rhea Royce,

73
00:04:55,920 --> 00:05:02,220
and Daemon calls Rhea his bronze b****, offering to give her to Otto as a replacement for his dead wife.

74
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:06,500
Otto almost loses his composure, and Daemon leaves the room with a smug smile on his face.

75
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:11,100
The next day, the tournament takes place with the announcement that Emma has gone into labor.

76
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:16,139
Finally! Anyway, many strong knights from all the different houses come forth and participate in the games,

77
00:05:16,439 --> 00:05:19,819
with many asking for the favor of the Targaryens to give them good fortune in their match.

78
00:05:22,509 --> 00:05:29,160
One of the knights, Ser Cristin Cole, an unknown Dornish knight, catches the attention of Rhaenyra.

79
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:32,199
Herald informs her that there is very little known about him,

80
00:05:32,459 --> 00:05:34,120
but he proves to be very handy with the blade.

81
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:41,360
Now, eventually, it's Daemon's turn to compete, and he chooses to compete against Ser Gwain Hightower, Otto's eldest son.

82
00:05:41,759 --> 00:05:45,379
Daemon fights dirty, and badly injures Gwain, and then, afterwards,

83
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:50,339
Daemon asks for Alicent to favor him good fortune in his next match, all while Otto watches.

84
00:05:50,779 --> 00:05:54,699
Eventually, it comes down to Daemon and Cristin as the two remaining knights, and surprisingly,

85
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:57,019
Cristin manages to knock Daemon off his horse.

86
00:05:57,439 --> 00:06:01,819
Daemon hates humiliation, so he challenges Cristin to continue their fight in a contest of arms.

87
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:05,379
The fight is brutal, but Cristin wins when he forces Daemon to yield.

88
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,339
Cristin then asks for the favor of Rhaenyra,

89
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,120
and she bashfully gives it to him.

90
00:06:09,379 --> 00:06:13,660
As the tournament continues, Viserys is informed, that Emma is experiencing labor complications.

91
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:18,019
He leaves the tournament and rushes to her aid, where he's informed there's no way to save them both,

92
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:19,180
and he will have to choose.

93
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:21,600
Will he save the boy, or save his wife?

94
00:06:21,959 --> 00:06:24,680
It's a choice that will set in motion the events that happen in the show,

95
00:06:24,939 --> 00:06:27,879
and he ends up choosing to save his son, naming him Balin.

96
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:30,939
Unfortunately, Balin dies just a few hours later,

97
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:36,019
and Viserys loses Emma, his son, and any hope of having a male heir in a matter of hours.

98
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:41,420
As their bodies are burned by dragon fire, the question of Viserys' successor becomes the most important topic.

99
00:06:41,699 --> 00:06:42,939
at the next small council meeting.

100
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:45,939
Corlys suggests Daemon, but given how reckless Daemon can be,

101
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:48,579
there's no guarantee the stability of the realm will be maintained.

102
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,180
So then the conversation comes back to Rhaenyra,

103
00:06:51,439 --> 00:06:53,319
or even Rhaenys as his successor.

104
00:06:53,740 --> 00:06:56,540
But Viserys is too swept up in grief to make a decision right now.

105
00:06:56,860 --> 00:06:59,339
Otto sees this as a chance to gain control of the throne,

106
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:07,000
and sends Alicent looking very pretty to provide comfort to Viserys, hoping this leads to, um, other things.

107
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:11,420
At first, Alicent doesn't like being used, or potentially one day becoming the stepmom.

108
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:14,980
to her best friend, but after seeing how sorrowful Viserys is,

109
00:07:15,459 --> 00:07:19,079
she empathizes with the loss of his wife by relating to him over the death of her mother.

110
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:23,319
Yeah, I bet this won't at all destroy Alicent's friendship with Rhaenyra.

111
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:28,800
Meanwhile, Daemon drowns his sorrows in a brothel he frequently visits, and drunkenly makes a toast to Balin,

112
00:07:29,079 --> 00:07:30,819
dubbing him the heir for a day.

113
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:34,360
Viserys gets pissed when he finds out, but Daemon defends his actions.

114
00:07:35,019 --> 00:07:39,079
You've only ever tried to send me away to the Vale, to the City Watch.

115
00:07:39,579 --> 00:07:44,480
Ten years you've been king, and yet not once have you asked me to be your hand.

116
00:07:44,699 --> 00:07:50,480
Nevertheless, Viserys sends Daemon back to Runestone in the Vale of Arryn, the ancestral home to House Royce,

117
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:54,079
officially stripping Daemon from ever having any chance at being Viserys' heir.

118
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:59,819
Daemon leaves, and Viserys notices he cut his finger on the Iron Throne, poetic symbolism at its finest.

119
00:07:59,839 --> 00:08:04,019
Later, Viserys speaks with Rhaenyra, their first conversation in a long time,

120
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:06,779
where he informs her that she will be his heir.

121
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:08,860
He apologizes for not naming her sooner.

122
00:08:09,199 --> 00:08:13,160
Well, I guess it's better late than ever, as they stand before the Skull of Beleriand.

123
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:15,860
Viserys' dragon, the last dragon to see old Valyria,

124
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:20,220
before the Doom, he makes her promise to not let the kingdom suffer the same fate.

125
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:24,519
The idea that we control the dragons is an illusion.

126
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:28,879
Viserys then reveals Aegon's dream about the Night King

127
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:31,579
and the White Walkers, which we saw in Game of Thrones.

128
00:08:32,019 --> 00:08:36,080
He warns Rhaenyra that if all of Westeros must stand together against this dangerous threat one day,

129
00:08:36,419 --> 00:08:38,740
a Targaryen must sit upon the Iron Throne.

130
00:08:39,059 --> 00:08:44,440
He adds that Aegon foresaw the prince that was promised, someone that will save everyone during this dark time,

131
00:08:44,679 --> 00:08:45,809
and that it will be a Targaryen.

132
00:08:46,419 --> 00:08:51,960
Rhaenyra promises to uphold this dream, and she's declared heir to the Iron Throne, the first woman in its history.

133
00:08:52,419 --> 00:08:57,960
Episode 2 begins six months later with a grotesque shot of what has recently happened in the Stepstones,

134
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:02,639
a chain of rocky islands between Westeros and Essos that provide a strategic naval trade route.

135
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:05,559
Kragas Drahar, Prince Admiral of the Triarchy,

136
00:09:05,899 --> 00:09:11,659
has just attacked a series of Westerosi ships and left the sailors to be eaten alive by crabs that washed in from the tide.

137
00:09:12,139 --> 00:09:15,659
Wow. It's no wonder this dude is also known as Crabfeeder.

138
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:20,799
Anyway, the Triarchy is an alliance of the three free cities of Lys, Myr, and Tyrosh,

139
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,740
also known as the Kingdom of the Three Daughters,

140
00:09:23,340 --> 00:09:26,539
and they now pose a threat to Westeros' economic and political stability.

141
00:09:26,899 --> 00:09:31,590
At the small council meeting, Corlys is outraged that Viserys has done nothing while his men are slaughtered,

142
00:09:31,759 --> 00:09:35,000
so Rhaenyra butts in and suggests they make a show of force with their dragons.

143
00:09:35,679 --> 00:09:38,279
Corlys likes this idea, but Viserys dismisses it,

144
00:09:38,559 --> 00:09:40,580
as starting a war is the last thing that he wants to do.

145
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:44,759
Viserys will do this a lot, hence why he's later dubbed Viserys the Peaceful.

146
00:09:45,299 --> 00:09:49,639
Viserys instead has herald escort Rhaenyra away to choose a new knight to join the Kingsguard.

147
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:55,440
From the selection of candidates, Rhaenyra realizes not a single one has any combat experience except for one, Criston.

148
00:09:55,879 --> 00:09:57,759
Smitten by him, Rhaenyra chooses Criston.

149
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:01,919
Otto suggests other candidates that belong to houses that would better benefit the realm,

150
00:10:02,279 --> 00:10:04,539
but he's outvoted by the future heir to the throne.

151
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:10,120
After the meeting, Corlys and Rhaenys inform Viserys that the reason why they are being challenged and attacked by neighboring

152
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:14,899
forces is because ever since a woman is named heir to the throne, people don't fear the Targaryens anymore.

153
00:10:15,299 --> 00:10:19,059
They suggest that Viserys marry their 12-year-old daughter, Lyanna,

154
00:10:19,759 --> 00:10:23,360
so that their houses would be united and could help strengthen their rule.

155
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:28,139
Viserys attempts to indulge the idea of marrying a child as his royal duty, but let's be honest,

156
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:30,820
surely there's another way for Viserys to strengthen the kingdom.

157
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,360
Please let there be another way.

158
00:10:32,519 --> 00:10:38,149
Later, Otto calls an emergency small council meeting, because Daemon, who has now declared himself the Prince of Dragonstone,

159
00:10:38,519 --> 00:10:42,840
the original Targaryen fortress, has stolen one of their dragon eggs kept under lock and key in the stable.

160
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:49,070
Apparently, before Daemon left King's Landing, he took with him the entire city's watch and a worker named Massaria.

161
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:54,440
She's now pregnant and wants their baby's cradle to have a dragon's egg in it, according to the Targaryen custom.

162
00:10:55,019 --> 00:10:57,139
Obviously, Daemon is doing this to provoke Viserys,

163
00:10:57,419 --> 00:10:59,259
so Viserys decides not to play Daemon's game.

164
00:10:59,519 --> 00:11:02,379
Until Viserys learns, Daemon took the egg that was going to be Bailyn's.

165
00:11:02,779 --> 00:11:06,960
Viserys sends Otto to Dragonstone and Otto scolds a patiently waiting Daemon for what he's done.

166
00:11:07,559 --> 00:11:13,620
Daemon refuses to give up the egg and forces Otto to back down when Daemon's dragon, Caraxes, enters the chat.

167
00:11:13,980 --> 00:11:19,440
Suddenly, Rhaenyra appears riding Sirax, giving Daemon that show of force that she was talking about earlier.

168
00:11:19,879 --> 00:11:22,100
She and Daemon speak the old Valerian tongue,

169
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:25,620
and she discovers that Massaria isn't pregnant, nor are they married.

170
00:11:26,059 --> 00:11:28,299
Basically, Daemon was just being Daemon.

171
00:11:34,009 --> 00:11:38,100
Rhaenyra reminds Daemon that if he wants the Iron Throne, then he should just kill her right here and now,

172
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:40,320
but instead, he gives Rhaenyra back the egg.

173
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:46,039
When Rhaenyra returns to King's Landing, Viserys scolds her for disobeying him, and for putting herself in harm's way,

174
00:11:46,399 --> 00:11:49,039
Rhaenyra claims she got the job done better than Otto would have done,

175
00:11:49,399 --> 00:11:52,559
and this makes Viserys realize that his little girl actually has grown up.

176
00:11:52,899 --> 00:11:54,759
Their conversation turns to Rhaenyra's mother,

177
00:11:55,059 --> 00:11:58,980
and Rhaenyra understands that Viserys will need to remarry to ensure their line is being defended.

178
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:02,299
She's happy for him, and hopes the best for him and whoever he chooses.

179
00:12:02,679 --> 00:12:06,679
So the next morning, at the next small council meeting, Viserys announces who he will marry.

180
00:12:07,139 --> 00:12:08,120
Alicent Hightower.

181
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:13,399
Turns out, Otto's plan worked, as Viserys and Alicent have been growing very close during all this time.

182
00:12:13,899 --> 00:12:17,539
Corlys is outraged that Viserys would choose to poison the pure Valyrian line of succession,

183
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:20,299
and Rhaenyra is hurt that her best friend will betray her like this.

184
00:12:20,659 --> 00:12:25,840
This is the final straw that pushes Corlys to create an alliance with Daemon to help deal with the Triarchy problem.

185
00:12:26,299 --> 00:12:28,259
Episode 3 begins three years later.

186
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:32,299
Daemon and Corlys have been fighting Crabfeeder and his forces these past three years,

187
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:35,299
and haven't come any closer to stopping him even with the aid of Caraxes.

188
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:39,960
Meanwhile, Viserys and Alicent have already married, making Alicent the queen, and by now,

189
00:12:40,139 --> 00:12:42,840
she has produced a male heir named Aegon.

190
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:44,139
With another one on the way.

191
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:47,039
Alicent has tried to mend her relationship with Rhaenyra,

192
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:49,240
but she still continues to give her the cold shoulder,

193
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:53,120
especially since Alicent's son knocked Rhaenyra back in line for the Iron Throne.

194
00:13:01,250 --> 00:13:05,220
Rhaenyra is now 17, so Viserys has suggested that she find a suitor to one day wed,

195
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:09,220
particularly somebody from an important house so they can form an alliance and protect their lineage.

196
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:12,759
Many suitors come forward, including Jace and Lannister.

197
00:13:13,139 --> 00:13:15,960
Not to be confused with his twin brother, Tyland Lannister.

198
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:19,460
At one point, Otto proposes that Rhaenyra marry Aegon.

199
00:13:24,110 --> 00:13:29,240
Boy just turned two, Otto, but it would cease the endless proposals for Rhaenyra's home.

200
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:32,379
Ironically, Otto was not joking.

201
00:13:32,799 --> 00:13:37,799
Rhaenyra gets fed up with everything that she leaves Aegon's second nameday celebration on her own.

202
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:41,059
Luckily, Kristen saw her run off, and he chased after her.

203
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:46,279
They come to a clearing, and Rhaenyra vents about her father showing more favoritism to Aegon than to her,

204
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:48,539
and being paraded around in front of suitors.

205
00:13:48,899 --> 00:13:51,500
Kristen offers to kill Jason for her, and it makes her laugh.

206
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:53,639
They end up bonding on the way back to camp.

207
00:13:54,019 --> 00:13:56,879
A few days later, Viserys realizes he hasn't been fair to his daughter.

208
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:59,360
He still insists that she marry somebody someday,

209
00:13:59,799 --> 00:14:00,899
but he lets her choose who that is.

210
00:14:01,419 --> 00:14:04,860
It makes her happy, because typically, only men get to choose who they marry.

211
00:14:05,179 --> 00:14:07,259
It's not the only change of heart Viserys had,

212
00:14:07,539 --> 00:14:10,990
as he has finally decided to offer aid to Daemon and Corlys in defeating Crabfeeder.

213
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:17,279
Enraged that Viserys is helping now after three years, Daemon acts as bait, pretending to surrender to Crabfeeder.

214
00:14:17,539 --> 00:14:22,559
He draws Crabfeeder and his forces out, and single-handedly cuts his way before being wounded by a few arrows.

215
00:14:22,879 --> 00:14:28,480
Surrounded, Corlys and his son, Laenor, come to his aid, unleashing the might of the dragons on Crabfeeder's army.

216
00:14:28,779 --> 00:14:32,659
Daemon kills Crabfeeder, and ends the war before Viserys' troops can arrive.

217
00:14:33,159 --> 00:14:35,080
Wow. Daemon is pretty badass.

218
00:14:35,659 --> 00:14:39,320
Episode 4 takes place one year later, and Rhaenyra has been touring Westeros,

219
00:14:39,539 --> 00:14:40,860
as she's still forced to find a suitor.

220
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:46,899
The process isn't very fun, as each man ranges from men older than Viserys to children younger than her.

221
00:14:47,259 --> 00:14:52,600
Ew. She returns to King's Landing, just as Daemon is returning from conquering most of the Stepstones and the Triarchy.

222
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:56,360
He wears a crown on his head, as his men named him King of the Narrow Sea,

223
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:58,299
but Daemon knows there is one true king,

224
00:14:58,659 --> 00:15:01,440
and offers Viserys' crown and the Stepstones to him.

225
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,759
Viserys is grateful, and welcomes his brother home.

226
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:06,100
I knew that they'd just forgive and forget.

227
00:15:06,539 --> 00:15:10,679
That night, Daemon invites Rhaenyra to sneak out of the castle disguised as a commoner,

228
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:13,620
and introduces her to the vile nightlife of King's Landing.

229
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:17,799
Their journeys take them to a brothel, where they finally give in to their feelings for one another.

230
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:22,059
However, Daemon has second thoughts about getting frisky with her in a public place, and abandons her.

231
00:15:22,519 --> 00:15:25,899
Did his conscience get the better of him, or could it be something else?

232
00:15:26,340 --> 00:15:30,899
Rhaenyra returns to the castle, and a confused Kristen, who has been standing guard outside her door,

233
00:15:31,179 --> 00:15:32,100
wonders where she came from.

234
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:33,919
He checks on her, and Rhaenyra ends up.

235
00:15:34,190 --> 00:15:34,960
Seducing Kristen.

236
00:15:35,340 --> 00:15:37,299
Despite trying to uphold his oath, he gives into it,

237
00:15:37,580 --> 00:15:38,759
and helps her lose her virginity.

238
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:43,320
The next day, one of Otto's contacts, who saw Daemon and Rhaenyra in the brothel, informs him about it,

239
00:15:43,419 --> 00:15:44,519
and Otto informs Viserys.

240
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:46,179
The news upsets him.

241
00:15:46,559 --> 00:15:50,480
Alysyn overheard everything, and questions Rhaenyra over what she did, and she wants to help Rhaenyra.

242
00:15:59,419 --> 00:16:02,980
Rhaenyra instead twists Alysyn's words, and denies that Daemon touched her at all.

243
00:16:03,259 --> 00:16:05,250
Alysyn believes her, and they reconcile their friendship.

244
00:16:05,639 --> 00:16:07,639
However, a hungover Daemon re-enters the castle,

245
00:16:07,899 --> 00:16:08,940
and is brought before Viserys.

246
00:16:09,419 --> 00:16:12,519
Daemon doesn't even deny what they did, and suggests that he and Rhaenyra might be wed.

247
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:15,600
Viserys refuses it, and once again sends him back to the Vale.

248
00:16:16,039 --> 00:16:20,779
Viserys then confronts Rhaenyra, knowing that she lied to Alysyn, and commands that she now marry Lann.

249
00:16:27,970 --> 00:16:30,620
The marriage would strengthen the unity between their two houses,

250
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:32,679
and combine their shared dragon and naval fleets.

251
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:34,220
No one would stand in their way.

252
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:39,360
Rhaenyra agrees to this, but only if Viserys finally realizes Otto has been playing him all this time.

253
00:16:39,779 --> 00:16:44,580
Viserys then confronts Otto, exposing his plan to have Alysyn comfort him as a calculated distraction,

254
00:16:44,919 --> 00:16:47,080
just so Otto could have Aegon ascend to the Iron Throne.

255
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,980
He thanks Otto for all he's done for the crown,

256
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:50,779
and then strips him of his title as Hand of the Throne.

257
00:16:51,419 --> 00:16:57,019
The episode ends with Viserys having the Grand Maester bring a tea to Rhaenyra's bedchamber that is supposed to help

258
00:16:57,019 --> 00:16:59,299
her have an abortion just in case.

259
00:16:59,980 --> 00:17:04,420
Episode 5 begins back at the Vale, with us finally meeting Daemon's wife, Lady Rhea.

260
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:08,839
At least for only a few minutes, because Daemon kills her, making it look like an accident.

261
00:17:09,539 --> 00:17:11,099
Sweetheart, we're married.

262
00:17:14,339 --> 00:17:14,839
Consider that a divorce.

263
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:20,960
Back at King's Landing, Otto is still leaving when Alysyn catches him apologizing for being responsible for losing his position.

264
00:17:21,299 --> 00:17:23,279
He blames her for believing that Rhaenyra told the truth,

265
00:17:23,579 --> 00:17:25,680
but Alysyn still believes that she was telling the truth.

266
00:17:26,059 --> 00:17:27,880
Otto then warns her that when Viserys is dead,

267
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:32,380
Rhaenyra will have no choice but to put Alysyn's children to death in order to secure her claim to the throne.

268
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:39,339
Either you prepare Aegon to rule, or you cleave to Rhaenyra and pray for her mercy.

269
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:44,200
Later, Alysyn is approached by Lerys Strong of House Strong, the soft-spoken,

270
00:17:44,319 --> 00:17:46,440
crippled son of the new Hand of the King, Lynel Strong.

271
00:17:46,799 --> 00:17:48,940
He offers his condolences to what happened to her father,

272
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:54,819
and then makes a backhanded inquiry about Rhaenyra's health when he mentions the tea that she was given the same night Daemon was exiled.

273
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:58,740
This causes Alysyn to suspect that Rhaenyra lied to her about her and Daemon.

274
00:17:59,039 --> 00:18:03,119
Meanwhile, Viserys and Rhaenyra arrive at Driftmark, the island seat of House Velaryon,

275
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:05,920
to propose the marriage between Rhaenyra and Laenor.

276
00:18:06,259 --> 00:18:09,319
Corlys loves this idea, but he's more concerned about how the succession will play out.

277
00:18:09,859 --> 00:18:11,660
Especially since Viserys now is a son.

278
00:18:12,019 --> 00:18:16,500
Viserys assures him that Rhaenyra will still inherit the Iron Throne, and her children, regardless of gender,

279
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:17,579
will succeed after her.

280
00:18:17,839 --> 00:18:22,720
To sweeten this deal, Viserys adds that their children will be born Valyrian, not Targaryen.

281
00:18:23,099 --> 00:18:24,420
At least until they ascend to the throne.

282
00:18:28,059 --> 00:18:33,380
Corlys accepts this proposal, despite knowing Laenor is gay,

283
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:35,599
so bearing an heir with a woman might be a little difficult.

284
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:40,380
Rhaenyra already suspects that he was, so they agree to do their duty for the stability of the realm,

285
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:42,460
and then secretly sleep with whoever they want.

286
00:18:42,779 --> 00:18:45,420
Wow. So a lavender marriage may end up saving the realm.

287
00:18:45,779 --> 00:18:47,880
Hmm. On the journey back to King's Landing,

288
00:18:48,119 --> 00:18:51,799
Kristen proposes that he and Rhaenyra run away with new identities and elope in Asos.

289
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:56,819
Rhaenyra declines it, as she loves the idea of Kristen just being her s*** paramour, and this upsets him.

290
00:18:57,019 --> 00:19:01,019
When they arrive at King's Landing, Alicent speaks with Kristen regarding Rhaenyra's relationship with Daemon,

291
00:19:01,319 --> 00:19:05,799
and Kristen misinterprets their conversation and confesses that he and Rhaenyra have been sleeping together.

292
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:11,019
Whoops. Rhaenyra and Laenor are finally married, and their union is accompanied by a huge celebration,

293
00:19:11,339 --> 00:19:15,480
during which Viserys makes a grand speech about how momentous the joining of these two houses are.

294
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:19,200
Suddenly, Alicent interrupts his speech and enters, wearing a green dress,

295
00:19:19,420 --> 00:19:22,299
which is the signal color for House Hightower's call to arms.

296
00:19:22,779 --> 00:19:25,779
This is basically Alicent saying that she still aligns with House Hightower,

297
00:19:26,119 --> 00:19:29,660
and in a way, strikes the first blow in a great war that is to come.

298
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:36,339
Daemon makes a surprise appearance after not being invited, and during the celebration, Rhaea's cousin accuses Daemon of killing her.

299
00:19:36,759 --> 00:19:42,359
Daemon denies this, and instead asserts his claim to inherit Runestone, as that was what Rhaea was promised.

300
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:44,740
She wonder why Daemon killed her.

301
00:19:45,019 --> 00:19:47,819
Daemon then joins the dancing and flirts with the much older Leanna,

302
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:50,579
and the two of them get married shortly after this.

303
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:53,759
She produces two twin girls for him, Bela and Rhaena.

304
00:20:03,890 --> 00:20:08,180
Later, Laenor's gay lover, Joffrey, figures out that Kristen is Rhaenyra's paramour.

305
00:20:08,460 --> 00:20:11,839
He then tries to blackmail Kristen, threatening to reveal a secret if Kristen reveals his.

306
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:17,519
Enraged, Kristen brutally murders Joffrey in front of the other guests, causing a panic and horrifying Laenor.

307
00:20:17,839 --> 00:20:20,839
During all this, Viserys, who's been dealing with a sickness throughout the season,

308
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:23,059
almost collapses as his nose starts to bleed.

309
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:23,839
Remember this?

310
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:24,839
Because it's very important.

311
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:29,299
Kristen leaves the celebration and is so ashamed of what he did that he tries to off himself,

312
00:20:29,599 --> 00:20:30,559
but Alicent stops him.

313
00:20:30,779 --> 00:20:32,660
This causes them to form an unlikely friendship,

314
00:20:33,019 --> 00:20:34,400
and later, a hidden romance.

315
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:41,079
Episode 6 begins 10 years later, with several characters now replaced with older actors to show the passage of time.

316
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:48,859
Rhaenyra now has three sons, Jace, Lucerys, Luke, and is just now giving birth to the third, Joffrey.

317
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:52,279
However, if you look closely at her children, they look nothing like Laenor,

318
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,539
but like a certain member of the Kingsguard.

319
00:20:54,970 --> 00:20:58,599
Actually, it's not Kristen, but this new guy, Ser Harwin Strong,

320
00:20:59,059 --> 00:21:01,420
the captain of the city's watch and the eldest son of Lionel.

321
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:06,220
Alicent has been doing everything in her power to convince everybody, including a now very old Viserys,

322
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:08,779
that Rhaenyra's children aren't born of pure Valyrian blood,

323
00:21:09,099 --> 00:21:10,680
but Viserys remains ignorant to it.

324
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:16,180
Alicent informs a now snobbish teenage Aegon that needs to prepare to dispute Rhaenyra's claim to the throne one day.

325
00:21:16,319 --> 00:21:19,539
Later, Jace is finally given the chance to tame his dragon, Vermax.

326
00:21:20,039 --> 00:21:23,240
As mentioned earlier, Targaryen children are bonded with a dragon at birth,

327
00:21:23,480 --> 00:21:25,400
and later able to tame them when they get older.

328
00:21:25,819 --> 00:21:30,559
Aegon has already tamed his dragon, Sunfire, but his younger brother, Aemond, never had a dragon to bond with,

329
00:21:30,859 --> 00:21:32,519
because there weren't any more dragons at the time.

330
00:21:32,839 --> 00:21:35,119
This meant that he had to wait and claim a dragon one day,

331
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:37,259
and the other kids always make fun of him for it.

332
00:21:40,099 --> 00:21:43,240
Behold, the pink dragon!

333
00:21:44,329 --> 00:21:45,900
I know I might have implied it already,

334
00:21:46,039 --> 00:21:48,839
but it's worth mentioning that these kids are always fighting against each other.

335
00:21:49,299 --> 00:21:52,400
Speaking of fighting, Rhaenyra and Alicent never really mended their relationship,

336
00:21:53,079 --> 00:21:56,279
especially since the birth of their children and the fighting over who has the claim to the throne.

337
00:21:56,559 --> 00:22:01,819
In a desperate attempt to quell this fighting, and the rumors that Rhaenyra's children aren't actually Laenor's,

338
00:22:02,099 --> 00:22:06,940
Rhaenyra proposes that Jace marry Alicent's daughter, Helena, in order to unite their families.

339
00:22:07,380 --> 00:22:10,420
Rhaenyra adds that if her dragon lays another egg, then it will be Aemond's.

340
00:22:10,900 --> 00:22:15,200
Alicent refuses this, but Viserys loves the idea because he's tired of his family fighting each other.

341
00:22:15,680 --> 00:22:17,099
Join hands and be stronger for it.

342
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:20,930
Do as you wish, husband, when I am cold in my grave.

343
00:22:21,700 --> 00:22:25,359
For fear of Harwin's secret getting out, Lionel decides to resign as Hand of the King.

344
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:31,069
Viserys refuses to accept his resignation, so Lionel has to help escort his son Harwin back to Harrenhal,

345
00:22:31,279 --> 00:22:32,960
as he's already banished him there to keep him safe.

346
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:37,299
Alicent then confides with Larys, as the two of them have become very close allies in the years since,

347
00:22:37,579 --> 00:22:39,400
and wishes that her father was still Hand of the King.

348
00:22:39,460 --> 00:22:43,240
Meanwhile, Laina has been having complications giving birth to Daemon's third child,

349
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:49,039
and the pain is so horrible that she has her dragon, Vhagar, the largest and oldest dragon still living,

350
00:22:49,599 --> 00:22:51,079
burn her alive.

351
00:22:51,700 --> 00:22:54,779
Whoa. The episode ends with two important things happening.

352
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:58,240
One, Rhaenyra moves her entire family to Dragonstone to be safe.

353
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:03,099
Two, Lionel and Harwin arrive at Harrenhal, but that night, Larys, his own son,

354
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:06,980
arranges to have them burned alive by some criminals that he recently recruited.

355
00:23:07,299 --> 00:23:10,000
Larys did this to inherit Harrenhal, and to gain favor with Alicent.

356
00:23:10,500 --> 00:23:14,599
Everyone attends Laina's funeral, and she's buried in the traditional Valerian way at Driftmar.

357
00:23:15,319 --> 00:23:18,740
It's a sad moment for everybody, especially for Rhaenys and her grandchildren.

358
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:21,019
Laenor is the most affected by Laina's death,

359
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:23,680
and at one point contemplates offing himself in the sea.

360
00:23:23,980 --> 00:23:28,660
With all the family finally together again, Viserys sees this as an opportunity to knight the family again,

361
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,799
and invites Daemon to come home to King's Landing.

362
00:23:31,099 --> 00:23:35,000
Daemon rejects it, as he's still grieving Laina's death and has had enough of his brother.

363
00:23:35,279 --> 00:23:37,559
He storms off to the beach, and Rhaenyra follows him.

364
00:23:37,940 --> 00:23:39,059
They walk and talk along the beach,

365
00:23:39,339 --> 00:23:42,660
and their conversation turns to that night in the brothel when Daemon abandoned her.

366
00:23:43,059 --> 00:23:45,299
Rhaenyra blames Daemon for every bad thing that's happened to her.

367
00:23:45,539 --> 00:23:48,319
Daemon argues his life has been just as much a tragedy as hers,

368
00:23:48,720 --> 00:23:50,559
and the two end up reconciling and kissing.

369
00:23:50,980 --> 00:23:56,119
They end up making love, keeping the Targaryen inbreeding tradition alive and well.

370
00:23:56,559 --> 00:23:59,819
During this time, Aemon gets the stupid idea to try and tame Vhagar,

371
00:24:00,339 --> 00:24:02,660
since Laina is dead and he no longer has a writer.

372
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:06,779
Miraculously, Aemon doesn't get burned alive and bravely gets Vhagar to serve him.

373
00:24:07,079 --> 00:24:10,700
He mounts Vhagar, finally experiencing the awesome wonder of riding a dragon.

374
00:24:11,019 --> 00:24:12,440
The other kids find out what Aemon did,

375
00:24:12,660 --> 00:24:16,019
and Rhaena is upset because she had planned to inherit Vhagar after her mother.

376
00:24:16,299 --> 00:24:19,440
Aemon scoffs, saying she should find a pig to ride instead,

377
00:24:19,940 --> 00:24:21,700
and this prompts Rhaena and Bela to attack him.

378
00:24:22,079 --> 00:24:25,339
Jace and Luke join the fight, and things get so brutal that Jace pulls a knife.

379
00:24:25,759 --> 00:24:31,039
Aemon knocks Jace down, so Luke grabs the knife and slices part of Aemon's face, taking out Aemon's left eye.

380
00:24:35,130 --> 00:24:37,420
Harold finally arrives and stops the fight.

381
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:39,900
He has Aemon attended to and takes the kids to their parents.

382
00:24:40,299 --> 00:24:44,960
There is blame, pointed at everybody, prompting Viserys to snap and scold his entire family,

383
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:47,279
begging for them to stop fighting amongst themselves.

384
00:24:47,660 --> 00:24:51,539
He orders everybody to apologize and move on, but Alicent demands a debt to be paid,

385
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:54,279
and tries to remove Luke's eye with a Valyrian steel blade.

386
00:24:54,579 --> 00:24:57,000
She lunges at Luke, but Rhaenyra defends her son,

387
00:24:57,299 --> 00:24:59,609
and Alicent ends up cutting her former best friend instead.

388
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:00,880
It's a shocking moment.

389
00:25:01,279 --> 00:25:04,039
So Aemon ends it by convincing his mother his debt was already paid.

390
00:25:04,400 --> 00:25:07,059
I may have lost an eye, but I gained a dragon.

391
00:25:08,180 --> 00:25:12,700
The next day, as everyone prepares to leave Driftmark, Rhaenyra proposes to Daemon that they marry each other.

392
00:25:13,180 --> 00:25:17,920
Daemon points out that Laenor is still alive, so Rhaenyra has Daemon seek the help of Laenor's new secret lover,

393
00:25:18,220 --> 00:25:19,720
Carl, to fake Laenor's death.

394
00:25:20,079 --> 00:25:24,700
They pretend to have Laenor burned alive, and then marry each other in a private traditional Targaryen ceremony.

395
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:28,119
The episode ends with an alive Laenor escaping from Driftmark with Carl.

396
00:25:28,619 --> 00:25:31,539
As a famous knight once said, the things we do for love.

397
00:25:32,140 --> 00:25:36,460
Episode 8 begins six years later, and Corlys just got gravely injured fighting in the Stepstones,

398
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:39,240
as the conflict Daemon resolved earlier has been reopened.

399
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:43,000
Corly's younger brother, Vaemond, who has been in Corly's shadow all this time,

400
00:25:43,299 --> 00:25:46,460
petitions King's Landing to make him Corly's heir to Driftmark.

401
00:25:46,779 --> 00:25:53,390
However, this would illegitimize Rhaenyra's Luke as heir to Driftmark, despite the fact that they technically are already illegitimate.

402
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:57,400
So a now-pregnant Rhaenyra and Daemon make their way to King's Landing to defend their claim.

403
00:25:57,519 --> 00:26:02,680
Sadly, in the past six years, Viserys' mental and physical health has declined so badly that he is bedridden,

404
00:26:03,039 --> 00:26:05,380
and is sick with a condition that is causing his skin to rot away.

405
00:26:05,779 --> 00:26:07,720
He can barely recognize his own brother and daughter,

406
00:26:08,019 --> 00:26:13,380
but to cheer him up, they introduce his new grandsons, Aegon, later known as Aegon the Younger, and Viserys,

407
00:26:13,759 --> 00:26:14,759
named after Rhaenyra's father.

408
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:21,240
Wait. If Rhaenyra married her uncle, how are they still considered grandchildren?

409
00:26:22,240 --> 00:26:22,740
Uh, right?

410
00:26:23,099 --> 00:26:26,319
During this, Jace and Luke visit the training grounds they used to train at when they were boys,

411
00:26:26,759 --> 00:26:28,339
and watch a deadly swordsman spar with Kristen.

412
00:26:28,779 --> 00:26:31,579
As if the white hair wasn't a dead giveaway, the eye badge certainly was.

413
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:34,519
So it turns out this incredibly agile warrior is a grown-up Aemond,

414
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:36,799
and he's still angry at Luke for taking away his eye.

415
00:26:37,380 --> 00:26:38,319
I don't give a s*** about Tornys.

416
00:26:38,980 --> 00:26:41,559
Nephews? Have you come to train?

417
00:26:43,329 --> 00:26:47,960
Rhaenyra then tries to get Rhaenys on her side by proposing two marriage arrangements with House Velaryon.

418
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:50,119
Her grandchildren will marry Rhaenyra's sons.

419
00:26:50,500 --> 00:26:51,319
This doesn't go well.

420
00:26:51,660 --> 00:26:54,039
That night, Rhaenyra visits Viserys in his chambers,

421
00:26:54,460 --> 00:26:56,720
and at first, Viserys mistakes Rhaenyra for Alicent.

422
00:26:57,180 --> 00:27:00,880
She brings back what he told her about Aegon's dream, and that by naming her as his heir,

423
00:27:01,059 --> 00:27:03,740
he hoped it would unite the realm, but all it's done is divide it.

424
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:07,480
She demands an answer from him, but he's too weak to answer, and it devastates her.

425
00:27:07,900 --> 00:27:10,279
The next day, Vaemon presents his petition to the court,

426
00:27:10,579 --> 00:27:12,819
while Otto speaks for Viserys, who is still in bed resting.

427
00:27:13,400 --> 00:27:16,940
Suddenly, Viserys enters the court, on his feet, shocking everybody.

428
00:27:17,380 --> 00:27:18,960
Viserys somehow makes his way to the throne,

429
00:27:19,200 --> 00:27:22,559
and expresses his confusion as to why they are still debating the line of succession.

430
00:27:22,940 --> 00:27:28,339
Viserys affirms Rhaenyra is still his heir, and Rhaenys confirms this, informing everybody of the two marriage arrangements.

431
00:27:29,019 --> 00:27:32,839
I guess Rhaenys liked Rhaenyra's plan, after all.

432
00:27:33,240 --> 00:27:36,740
Vaemon is outraged by this, and calls Rhaenyra's children bastards,

433
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:38,900
so Daemon beheads him.

434
00:27:39,579 --> 00:27:41,400
At night, everyone gathers around for dinner,

435
00:27:41,579 --> 00:27:44,539
and tensions are still very high from everything that's happened in the past years.

436
00:27:44,880 --> 00:27:46,640
Viserys knows he doesn't have long left to live,

437
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:49,339
and he's more upset by how much fighting is happening amongst his family.

438
00:27:49,700 --> 00:27:52,359
He wants this time to be a moment of celebration for Jace and Luke,

439
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:54,700
as they prepare to one day marry Bela and Rhaena,

440
00:27:55,019 --> 00:27:57,000
but above all, he wants them all to forget the past,

441
00:27:57,400 --> 00:27:58,640
and learn to love one another again.

442
00:27:59,039 --> 00:28:03,259
Then, in a powerful moment, he takes his mask off that was hiding his disfigured face,

443
00:28:03,700 --> 00:28:06,160
so that everyone will see that these wishes are not of their king,

444
00:28:06,460 --> 00:28:07,740
but their father and grandfather.

445
00:28:08,380 --> 00:28:12,039
Set aside your grievances, if not for the sake of the crown,

446
00:28:12,720 --> 00:28:16,440
and for the sake of this old man, who loves you all

447
00:28:17,119 --> 00:28:17,750
so dearly.

448
00:28:19,140 --> 00:28:21,700
Rhaenyra takes the first step, and makes a toast to Alicent,

449
00:28:21,940 --> 00:28:24,259
praising her on how good she's been to her father through everything.

450
00:28:24,740 --> 00:28:29,160
Alicent is overwhelmed hearing this, and surprisingly raises a glass to her former best friend.

451
00:28:29,519 --> 00:28:31,240
The children then take turns doing the same,

452
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:35,400
and pretty soon, everybody's laughing and dancing together like one big happy family.

453
00:28:35,799 --> 00:28:39,519
It's all Viserys ever wanted, a rare moment of happiness in a Game of Thrones show,

454
00:28:39,839 --> 00:28:43,859
yet I can't help but think this is the last time the family is going to be like this.

455
00:28:44,220 --> 00:28:48,059
Later, Viserys is escorted back to bed, and Aemond, who has been quiet all this time,

456
00:28:48,059 --> 00:28:48,059
is a very happy family.

457
00:28:48,559 --> 00:28:50,920
sees Luke laughing at him, and slams his fist into the table.

458
00:28:51,460 --> 00:28:55,099
He then makes the final toast to the health of his nephews, it's clearly not a compliment,

459
00:28:55,339 --> 00:28:57,059
and the fighting between the boys continues.

460
00:28:57,740 --> 00:28:58,940
I knew it wasn't going to last.

461
00:28:59,440 --> 00:29:01,900
As the hour grows late, Alicent tends to a dying Viserys.

462
00:29:02,460 --> 00:29:04,720
Now this time, Viserys mistakes her for Rhaenyra.

463
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:07,819
He recalls the conversation he had with Rhaenyra about Aegon's dream,

464
00:29:08,140 --> 00:29:12,220
and Alicent mistakes this as Viserys naming their son Aegon as the prince who was promised,

465
00:29:12,619 --> 00:29:14,420
or in this case, the heir to the throne.

466
00:29:15,019 --> 00:29:21,779
Alicent understands, and then Viserys, first of his name, dies, calling out to his late wife, Emma.

467
00:29:22,339 --> 00:29:28,420
Episode 9 begins the same night, with one of the servant boys informing Alicent's handmaiden, Talia, that Viserys is dead.

468
00:29:28,819 --> 00:29:32,200
She then informs Alicent, who tells Otto, adding that Viserys, quote unquote,

469
00:29:32,700 --> 00:29:34,380
told her that her son Aegon was to be king.

470
00:29:34,779 --> 00:29:39,400
They inform the small council, which now consists of Tyland Lannister and Grand Maester Orwyle,

471
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:41,400
about Aegon now being the rightful ruler.

472
00:29:41,700 --> 00:29:45,299
Apparently, Tyland and Orwyle have already been scheming to have Aegon be king,

473
00:29:45,619 --> 00:29:46,660
so they're completely on board.

474
00:29:46,960 --> 00:29:51,940
But the elderly master of coin, Lyman Beesbury, doesn't believe Viserys changed his mind so easily.

475
00:29:52,160 --> 00:29:56,059
He starts accusing everybody of treachery, until Kristen shuts him up, accidentally killing him.

476
00:29:56,299 --> 00:29:59,880
This causes Herald to draw a sword on Kristen, and demand that he surrender as a king's guard.

477
00:30:00,259 --> 00:30:01,700
But Alicent tells them all to stand down.

478
00:30:02,119 --> 00:30:04,220
The conversation then turns to what to do with Rhaenyra,

479
00:30:04,559 --> 00:30:06,680
who along with all of her family have already left for Dragonstone.

480
00:30:07,180 --> 00:30:09,480
It is obvious she and Daemon never agree to this,

481
00:30:09,880 --> 00:30:11,299
or bend the knee to Aegon.

482
00:30:11,579 --> 00:30:14,240
So the only solution is to kill Rhaenyra and her household.

483
00:30:14,799 --> 00:30:15,740
Alicent objects to this.

484
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:18,420
But Otto orders Herald to take the Kingsguard and kill them.

485
00:30:18,799 --> 00:30:22,319
But Herald, disgusted by everything, resigns as the Lord Commander of the Kingsguard.

486
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:24,319
Kristen later becomes the new Lord Commander.

487
00:30:24,779 --> 00:30:27,279
Helena and Aemond are informed of Viserys' death.

488
00:30:27,640 --> 00:30:31,000
But Aegon is nowhere to be found, no doubt off on another of his vulgar adventures.

489
00:30:31,720 --> 00:30:39,119
In the meantime, Otto has Rhaenus and everyone else associated with the noble houses imprisoned or hanged until they switch their allegiances to Aegon.

490
00:30:39,619 --> 00:30:44,619
Otto sends two members of the Kingsguard, named Sir Eryk, and his twin brother, Eryk, to find Aegon.

491
00:30:45,299 --> 00:30:48,180
But Alicent sends Kristen to find him, and Aemond goes with him.

492
00:30:48,599 --> 00:30:50,900
Aemond already has a pretty good idea where Aegon is,

493
00:30:51,220 --> 00:30:52,839
and takes Kristen to Aegon's favorite brothel.

494
00:30:53,500 --> 00:30:53,960
Of course.

495
00:30:54,440 --> 00:30:57,539
Along the way, Aemond argues he's the stronger candidate for the throne,

496
00:30:57,680 --> 00:30:59,920
especially since he wants the throne more than Aegon does.

497
00:31:00,359 --> 00:31:03,420
In search of a wastrel who's never taken half an interest in his birthright.

498
00:31:03,680 --> 00:31:04,619
Desire he should be...

499
00:31:06,549 --> 00:31:08,119
Ironically, Aegon isn't there.

500
00:31:08,519 --> 00:31:10,619
So Aemond and Kristen wander the streets,

501
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:14,259
until they see Eryk and Otto speaking with a woman known as the White Worm,

502
00:31:14,559 --> 00:31:16,819
revealed to be Daemon's old mistress, Messaria.

503
00:31:17,480 --> 00:31:19,599
She is Aegon tucked away in the Grand Septa,

504
00:31:20,119 --> 00:31:24,160
and will give him up if Otto promises to end the Child Fighting Pits in Flea Bottom,

505
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:25,819
the poorest district in King's Landing.

506
00:31:26,299 --> 00:31:29,160
Otto promises, and the twins find Aegon stuffed inside a temple.

507
00:31:29,420 --> 00:31:32,119
As they exit, Aegon and Kristen draw their swords on them,

508
00:31:32,380 --> 00:31:34,799
and forcibly take Aegon back to the castle instead of them.

509
00:31:35,259 --> 00:31:41,019
Back at the castle, Larys informs Alyson of the network of spies within her servants, including Talia working for Messaria,

510
00:31:41,440 --> 00:31:43,180
and Alyson approves eliminating the network.

511
00:31:43,539 --> 00:31:47,519
Of course, he only reveals this information when she indulges his fetish for feet.

512
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:53,599
Okay? I mean, I guess it's not the weirdest thing to happen in this show?

513
00:31:54,039 --> 00:31:58,220
Early in the morning of Aegon's coronation, Eryk frees Rhaenys, as he's still loyal to her.

514
00:31:58,539 --> 00:31:59,559
He tries to get her to the city,

515
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:03,289
but they become separated as soldiers heard civilians of the coronation at Dragonpit.

516
00:32:03,700 --> 00:32:09,059
During which, Rhaenys makes her way into the caverns underneath Dragonpit and boards her dragon, Meles.

517
00:32:09,599 --> 00:32:12,160
She then crashes the coronation by rising up from the ground below.

518
00:32:12,599 --> 00:32:17,119
She contemplates this one chance to burn Alyson and her children, but decides not to,

519
00:32:17,380 --> 00:32:17,700
and leaves.

520
00:32:18,319 --> 00:32:21,559
Who says the queen who never was doesn't know how to be a badass.

521
00:32:22,220 --> 00:32:28,160
The last episode of season one begins with Rhaenys arriving at Dragonstone to inform Rhaenyra and the others that Viserys

522
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:29,980
is dead, and Aegon is now the king.

523
00:32:30,400 --> 00:32:32,400
Rhaenys explains she didn't bend the knee to Aegon,

524
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:34,779
but that Alyson will make sure they are all killed.

525
00:32:35,460 --> 00:32:37,240
The greens are coming for you, Rhaenyra.

526
00:32:37,960 --> 00:32:39,420
And for your children.

527
00:32:40,529 --> 00:32:43,319
The news shatters Rhaenyra so much that she has a miscarriage.

528
00:32:44,039 --> 00:32:48,480
As they cremate their stillborn, Eryk arrives, having abandoned the Kingsguard and his twin brother,

529
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:50,519
and presents Rhaenyra with Viserys' crown.

530
00:32:50,880 --> 00:32:54,240
He pledges allegiance to Rhaenyra, the one true queen,

531
00:32:54,799 --> 00:32:58,339
and Daemon places it upon Rhaenyra's head, declaring her his queen as well.

532
00:32:58,740 --> 00:33:02,819
Their next step is to gather as many allies and houses as they can because it's obvious a war is coming.

533
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:04,619
But then Otto arrives delivering a message.

534
00:33:05,259 --> 00:33:09,579
Rhaenyra and her family will be allowed to possess Dragonstone if they declare Aegon as the one true king.

535
00:33:09,960 --> 00:33:13,259
Daemon is the first one to reject this, and Rhaenyra calls Otto a traitor.

536
00:33:13,779 --> 00:33:16,519
Swords are drawn, but Rhaenyra prevents more bloodshed from happening,

537
00:33:16,819 --> 00:33:19,119
and assures Otto that Alyson will have her answer tomorrow.

538
00:33:19,339 --> 00:33:25,119
Later, Daemon pressures Rhaenyra to go to war with Aegon because they have already declared war on them.

539
00:33:25,539 --> 00:33:29,819
Daemon reminds her that they have the support of House Stark, Tully, and Baratheon on their side.

540
00:33:30,079 --> 00:33:32,240
Not to mention twice as many dragons as Aegon has,

541
00:33:32,500 --> 00:33:34,240
but Rhaenyra refuses to be queen of the ashes.

542
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:39,180
Rhaenyra would rather try and unify the realm, reminding Daemon of Aegon's dream,

543
00:33:39,500 --> 00:33:41,039
but all it does is anger Daemon more.

544
00:33:41,460 --> 00:33:46,259
Meanwhile, Corlys finally awakens from his injuries, and Rhaenys catches him up to speed on all that's happened,

545
00:33:46,779 --> 00:33:47,660
including the death of his brother.

546
00:33:48,140 --> 00:33:51,180
Corlys begins to wonder if they should abandon trying to pursue the Iron Throne,

547
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:55,960
and is quick to point out to Rhaenyra that there's no guarantee the houses that support her will continue to do so.

548
00:33:56,319 --> 00:34:01,799
Nevertheless, Corlys offers the full support of his house and his fleet to Rhaenyra, including the support of the Triarchy.

549
00:34:02,279 --> 00:34:04,619
This means they can cut off all sea trade to King's Landing,

550
00:34:05,079 --> 00:34:08,659
and eventually lay siege to King's Landing from the sea, forcing Alicent to surrender.

551
00:34:09,159 --> 00:34:12,699
Jace then volunteers he and Luke to fly to the north and make sure House Stark, Tully,

552
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:14,300
and Baratheon are still loyal.

553
00:34:14,460 --> 00:34:16,420
They might just have the edge to win this thing.

554
00:34:16,679 --> 00:34:19,320
Luke arrives at Storm's End, the home of House Baratheon,

555
00:34:19,699 --> 00:34:24,260
and discovers that Aemond is already there, asking for Lord Boris Baratheon to bend the knee to Aegon.

556
00:34:25,059 --> 00:34:28,579
Aemond's offer is better than Luke's, so Boris allies himself with Aegon.

557
00:34:28,800 --> 00:34:31,639
Defeated, Luke begins to leave, but Aemond is not done with him.

558
00:34:32,079 --> 00:34:33,840
He refers to Luke as House Strong,

559
00:34:34,340 --> 00:34:38,059
and will allow Rhaenyra to have House Baratheon if Luke removes one of his eyes.

560
00:34:38,679 --> 00:34:40,780
Luke made a promise to his mother that he wouldn't start a fight,

561
00:34:41,139 --> 00:34:42,219
so he leaves on his dragon.

562
00:34:42,639 --> 00:34:47,059
Aemond chases Luke on Vhagar through an intense storm, simply to toy with them.

563
00:34:47,280 --> 00:34:48,809
But both of them lose control of their dragons,

564
00:34:49,239 --> 00:34:52,159
and Vhagar disobeys Aemond, killing both Luke and his dragon.

565
00:34:52,449 --> 00:34:56,300
Aemond is shocked, and realizes he may have just started the war Rhaenyra didn't want.

566
00:34:56,739 --> 00:34:58,460
What was that that Viserys said in the beginning?

567
00:34:58,800 --> 00:35:01,119
The idea that we control the dragons is an illusion.

568
00:35:01,719 --> 00:35:02,940
It all makes sense now.

569
00:35:03,579 --> 00:35:08,559
The first episode of Season 2 begins at The Wall, where Jace is meeting with the leader of House Stark,

570
00:35:08,860 --> 00:35:11,500
Cregan Stark, about joining forces with Rhaenyra.

571
00:35:11,920 --> 00:35:15,980
Cregan can't join the fight, because he needs to prioritize making sure the Wall is heavily fortified,

572
00:35:16,340 --> 00:35:19,159
so he instead sends 2,000 soldiers to aid Rhaenyra's fight.

573
00:35:19,519 --> 00:35:21,530
As the old saying goes, the North remembers.

574
00:35:22,219 --> 00:35:27,559
Back at Dragonstone, a tired Rhaenys returns after securing the Valyrian shipping blockade in the gullet,

575
00:35:28,019 --> 00:35:30,119
the body of water between Dragonstone and Driftmark.

576
00:35:30,559 --> 00:35:34,840
Daemon doesn't care that she's tired, and wants her to accompany him in killing Aemond and Vhagar,

577
00:35:35,139 --> 00:35:36,079
so they can avenge Luke.

578
00:35:36,500 --> 00:35:38,219
Daemon wants to take a son for a son.

579
00:35:38,659 --> 00:35:42,480
Rhaenys decides to wait for Rhaenyra to command her, as she knows what it's like to lose a child.

580
00:35:43,099 --> 00:35:46,780
Daemon then blames Rhaenys for not killing Aegon and everyone else when she had the chance.

581
00:35:47,260 --> 00:35:49,880
During all of this, Corlys is still mourning the death of Luke,

582
00:35:50,179 --> 00:35:51,659
and checks in on the repairs to his ship,

583
00:35:52,059 --> 00:35:54,320
as it is still under repair from the battle that injured him.

584
00:35:54,559 --> 00:35:56,380
He speaks with one of the sailors, Alan,

585
00:35:56,679 --> 00:36:00,820
who assures him that the ship will be ready soon so Corlys can lead the effort in patrolling the gullet.

586
00:36:01,219 --> 00:36:03,760
Alan was also the one that rescued Corlys when he was injured,

587
00:36:04,039 --> 00:36:05,460
so Corlys is very fond of him.

588
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:09,139
When I mean fond, it's because Alan is Corlys' bastard son.

589
00:36:09,539 --> 00:36:14,579
Back at King's Landing, Aegon informs the small council that he wants to attack Rhaenyra with the full force of their dragons.

590
00:36:15,079 --> 00:36:18,119
Otto advises against this, and urges Aegon to learn the word restraint.

591
00:36:19,099 --> 00:36:22,860
Alicent stands by her father, as the last thing they need is Aegon getting killed on the battlefield.

592
00:36:23,500 --> 00:36:26,840
Later, Aegon tends to the grievances of the common people of King's Landing.

593
00:36:27,340 --> 00:36:32,739
He's very merciful, and generous at first, until Otto discreetly gives Aegon a lesson in maintaining order as a king.

594
00:36:33,059 --> 00:36:36,019
One of the grievances that comes forward belongs to a blacksmith named Hugh.

595
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:41,099
He, along with the other blacksmiths, have been working around the clock to build several large dragon-killing weapons,

596
00:36:41,300 --> 00:36:44,179
known as scorpions, to combat a possible dragon attack,

597
00:36:44,460 --> 00:36:46,389
but lately, they've been running low on supplies.

598
00:36:46,880 --> 00:36:49,239
Hugh is an honorable man, with a wife and sick daughter,

599
00:36:49,559 --> 00:36:51,760
so if anyone deserves to have his grievances heard, it's him.

600
00:36:52,239 --> 00:36:55,500
Aegon disregards Otto's advice, and grants Hugh his request.

601
00:36:56,039 --> 00:37:00,639
Larys sees this unfold, and afterwards gives Aegon the idea of getting rid of Otto's Hand of the King,

602
00:37:00,960 --> 00:37:04,099
as a way of distinguishing himself as a different king than Viserys.

603
00:37:04,380 --> 00:37:07,300
Meanwhile, it's revealed that Messaria survived the brothel fire,

604
00:37:07,599 --> 00:37:11,800
and is brought to Dragonstone, where Daemon is annoyed to learn that she has been the White Worm.

605
00:37:12,420 --> 00:37:14,800
He calls her a traitor for helping put Aegon on the throne,

606
00:37:15,139 --> 00:37:17,440
but she argues that she holds no loyalties to Aegon,

607
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:19,789
and everything she did was purely transactional.

608
00:37:20,280 --> 00:37:23,739
Daemon then offers her her freedom, in exchange for helping him kill Aemond.

609
00:37:23,960 --> 00:37:27,739
So, with Messaria's help, Daemon hires a rat-catcher nicknamed Cheese,

610
00:37:28,159 --> 00:37:31,440
and a city watchguard named Blood, to sneak into the Red Keep and kill Aemond.

611
00:37:33,019 --> 00:37:34,219
Should be easy enough to find.

612
00:37:35,820 --> 00:37:38,239
But I understand that he's quite good in a fight, you want to take caution?

613
00:37:38,750 --> 00:37:44,179
However, they aren't able to find Aemond, and instead find Helena with her twin children, Jaehaerys

614
00:37:44,460 --> 00:37:46,699
and Jaehaerah, which she had with Aegon.

615
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:50,920
They figure killing the king's son and heir to the throne will settle the son-for-a-son debt,

616
00:37:50,980 --> 00:37:55,960
so they behead Jaehaerys, while a traumatized Helena escapes with Jaehaerah to Alyson's room,

617
00:37:56,280 --> 00:37:59,539
where she finds Alyson and Kristen secretly making love in her bed.

618
00:37:59,900 --> 00:38:01,639
I don't know if this is awkward or just sad.

619
00:38:02,239 --> 00:38:05,639
Episode 2 begins with the Red Keep in chaos following the Jaehaerys murder.

620
00:38:06,119 --> 00:38:08,460
Aegon is devastated, and declares war on Rhaenyra.

621
00:38:09,039 --> 00:38:11,139
Aemond investigates how Cheese and Blood entered the Keep,

622
00:38:11,380 --> 00:38:13,340
and discovers one of the coins used as part of their payment.

623
00:38:13,739 --> 00:38:15,639
He suspects that he was the original target,

624
00:38:16,039 --> 00:38:19,119
and he is remorseful for Luke, blaming himself even more for what happened.

625
00:38:19,739 --> 00:38:23,340
Jaehaerys' death makes Aegon's rise to the throne seem even more like a bad omen,

626
00:38:23,639 --> 00:38:27,260
so Otto suggests they parade Jaehaerys' body through the streets and have a public funeral,

627
00:38:27,639 --> 00:38:29,460
in order to make Rhaenyra seem like more of a monster.

628
00:38:29,980 --> 00:38:32,630
On a bright note, they manage to capture Blood, so he's tortured,

629
00:38:32,760 --> 00:38:36,579
and confesses that Daemon hired him and a rat catcher he didn't know his name.

630
00:38:36,940 --> 00:38:40,000
During the procession, a herald chants, Rhaenyra the Cruel.

631
00:38:40,440 --> 00:38:43,679
His people line in the street to offer their condolences to Alyson and Helena.

632
00:38:44,159 --> 00:38:49,840
The whole process is hard for Helena, because she's socially awkward and known as a dragon dreamer.

633
00:38:50,219 --> 00:38:55,059
Afterwards, Aegon and Kristen have every rat catcher in the area hanged for everybody to see,

634
00:38:55,300 --> 00:38:57,260
as Blood never knew who his accomplice was.

635
00:38:57,760 --> 00:39:02,159
Otto finds out, and he's furious, because if this doesn't turn the people against Aegon, nothing will.

636
00:39:02,599 --> 00:39:05,980
Aegon argues that Kristen has done more to avenge his son's death than Otto has,

637
00:39:06,280 --> 00:39:08,980
and strips Otto of his title as Hand of the King, giving it to Kristen.

638
00:39:09,500 --> 00:39:11,900
Back at Dragonstone, Rhaenyra hears about what happened,

639
00:39:12,179 --> 00:39:13,980
and that she's being accused of something she didn't do.

640
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:16,539
She immediately suspects Daemon is responsible for this,

641
00:39:16,820 --> 00:39:19,820
but Daemon explains he was just trying to get Daemon killed, not Jaehaerys.

642
00:39:20,239 --> 00:39:22,940
Regardless of the mistake, Rhaenyra can't trust Daemon anymore,

643
00:39:23,300 --> 00:39:25,659
and accuses him of using her to gain the throne he always wanted.

644
00:39:26,079 --> 00:39:27,340
Enraged, Daemon flies, and he's not a good idea.

645
00:39:29,260 --> 00:39:33,079
Rhaenyra then questions Masaria after Daemon said that she was also responsible,

646
00:39:33,719 --> 00:39:38,360
and recognizes her as Daemon's former mistress, whom he claimed he already married and was having a child with.

647
00:39:38,679 --> 00:39:41,239
The logical thing would be for Rhaenyra to execute Masaria,

648
00:39:41,599 --> 00:39:45,260
but Masaria argues that she can still be useful to her because she is resourceful.

649
00:39:45,820 --> 00:39:48,119
Realizing they both have a common enemy, the Hightowers,

650
00:39:48,440 --> 00:39:52,960
and both have been hurt by the same man, Daemon, Rhaenyra decides to let her live and freeze her.

651
00:39:53,300 --> 00:39:56,980
Women supporting women, in a show with a lot of violence towards women.

652
00:39:57,480 --> 00:39:59,679
As Masaria leaves, she sees Arric arrive,

653
00:40:00,099 --> 00:40:03,900
and realizes he's been sent by Kristen to impersonate his twin brother and kill Rhaenyra.

654
00:40:04,300 --> 00:40:08,139
Arric makes it to a sleeping Rhaenyra, but luckily, Arric arrives and fights his brother.

655
00:40:08,440 --> 00:40:10,260
He defends his queen, and kills his brother.

656
00:40:10,519 --> 00:40:14,440
Sadly, Arric feels so guilty for what he did that he decides to fall on his own sword.

657
00:40:15,159 --> 00:40:17,019
Episode 3 begins in The Riverlands,

658
00:40:17,420 --> 00:40:22,480
where we see a few brackens and blackwoods get into a minor dispute regarding boundary stones that eventually unravels into

659
00:40:22,480 --> 00:40:25,039
a massive battle that kills tens of thousands of men.

660
00:40:25,260 --> 00:40:28,719
It's worth noting that the Brackens side with Aegon, while the Blackwood side with Rhaenyra.

661
00:40:29,099 --> 00:40:34,000
In a way, this feud is a classic example for what will happen between Rhaenyra and Alicent if they don't reconcile.

662
00:40:36,389 --> 00:40:40,460
To make sure they keep the Riverlands in check,

663
00:40:40,780 --> 00:40:45,079
Kristen proposes to the small council the idea of enlisting the Brackens and conquering what's left of Harrenhal.

664
00:40:45,300 --> 00:40:47,880
He plans to take Aemond, and Aegon wants to go with Sunfire,

665
00:40:48,219 --> 00:40:49,300
but everyone advises against it.

666
00:40:49,780 --> 00:40:52,940
Before Kristen leaves, Alicent has her brother, Gwaine, accompany him.

667
00:40:53,400 --> 00:40:57,139
Gwaine is pleased to come with him, but is confused as to how Kristen, nobody from Dorne,

668
00:40:57,320 --> 00:40:59,119
was able to ascend to the Hand of the King so quickly.

669
00:40:59,780 --> 00:41:03,039
Kristen dismisses it, then asks for Alicent to grant him favor in his battle,

670
00:41:03,480 --> 00:41:05,960
like how the knights did during the tournament in Season 1, Episode 1.

671
00:41:06,380 --> 00:41:10,659
Alicent gives Kristen her handkerchief, and Gwaine sees this, putting the pieces together.

672
00:41:10,980 --> 00:41:16,539
Meanwhile, Daemon arrives in Harrenhal and finds the place eerily empty, save for a few members of House Strong.

673
00:41:16,980 --> 00:41:19,699
The Castellan, or Warden of Harrenhal, Simon Strong,

674
00:41:20,199 --> 00:41:24,739
pledges himself to Rhaenyra without any trouble since the majority of the House Strong hold no loyalty to Larys,

675
00:41:25,099 --> 00:41:27,260
and believe he started the fire that killed his father.

676
00:41:27,659 --> 00:41:30,699
During his time at Harrenhal, Daemon has visions and dreams about his past,

677
00:41:31,179 --> 00:41:31,960
and how he will die.

678
00:41:32,380 --> 00:41:34,940
A witch named Alice constantly haunts him there,

679
00:41:35,280 --> 00:41:37,039
and he develops a love-hate relationship with her.

680
00:41:37,500 --> 00:41:40,179
Aside from trying to unite the Blackwoods and Brackens to fight for Rhaenyra,

681
00:41:40,480 --> 00:41:43,659
all Daemon does the rest of the season is have visions and interact with Alice,

682
00:41:43,820 --> 00:41:46,780
so I'm just not really going to talk about it, it's not very interesting.

683
00:41:47,179 --> 00:41:50,980
In one of the brothels in King's Landing, we meet one of the fast-talking patrons, Ulf,

684
00:41:51,440 --> 00:41:56,159
telling his friends about how his father was Viserys and Daemon's brother, Baelin, making him a Targaryen.

685
00:41:56,500 --> 00:42:00,280
Apparently, Targaryens visiting brothels and knocking at prostitutes was a pretty common thing,

686
00:42:00,579 --> 00:42:03,920
so who knows how many bastard Targaryen children roam the streets of King's Landing?

687
00:42:04,139 --> 00:42:06,519
Of course, there's no way to know, so what good is Ulf's word?

688
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:10,000
Meanwhile, Rhaenyra and Baelia ride out and patrol the Riverlands,

689
00:42:10,300 --> 00:42:13,139
and Baelia eventually spots Kristen and his men making their way to Harrenhal.

690
00:42:13,659 --> 00:42:17,619
She descends upon them, prompting Kristen and the others to race to the nearby trees for cover,

691
00:42:17,980 --> 00:42:18,739
making it just in time.

692
00:42:19,300 --> 00:42:22,000
Baelia loses them and leaves, reporting back to Rhaenyra.

693
00:42:22,500 --> 00:42:27,800
Rhaenyra's advisors argue that peace is no longer an option if Aegon's armies are trying to claim Harrenhal,

694
00:42:28,099 --> 00:42:29,900
but Rhaenyra still believes war can be averted.

695
00:42:30,280 --> 00:42:34,159
With Masaria's help, who has now become Rhaenyra's closest advisor since she spotted Arric,

696
00:42:34,440 --> 00:42:37,579
Rhaenyra sneaks herself into King's Landing so she can secretly speak with Alicent.

697
00:42:38,059 --> 00:42:41,460
She disguises herself as one of the female clergy, known as a Septa,

698
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:44,320
and comes to Alicent while she is praying in the Grand Septa.

699
00:42:45,179 --> 00:42:46,139
Alicent is shocked to see her,

700
00:42:46,440 --> 00:42:50,079
and Rhaenyra explains she's here so they can come to terms and prevent an unnecessary war.

701
00:42:50,480 --> 00:42:54,659
Their conversation turns into Viserys' last words, and Alicent mentions Aegon's dream.

702
00:42:55,079 --> 00:42:59,280
Rhaenyra realizes what Viserys meant, that Alicent made a mistake naming Aegon as the rightful heir.

703
00:42:59,639 --> 00:43:01,579
Alicent tells Rhaenyra it is too late for peace,

704
00:43:02,000 --> 00:43:02,300
and leaves.

705
00:43:03,099 --> 00:43:06,039
Episode 4 begins with Kristen claiming Duskendale for Aegon,

706
00:43:06,340 --> 00:43:09,579
and beheading Lord Duncan Darklyn when he won't bend the knee to Aegon.

707
00:43:09,940 --> 00:43:15,519
Kristen then receives new secret orders from Aemond, telling him to forget Harrenhal and attack Rook's Rest near Blackwater Bay,

708
00:43:15,760 --> 00:43:16,829
which is home to House Staunton.

709
00:43:17,199 --> 00:43:22,360
House Staunton is still loyal to Rhaenyra, and if they conquer Rook's Rest, Dragonstone will officially be cut off.

710
00:43:22,739 --> 00:43:28,119
Aegon finds out Kristen and Aemond have been plotting behind his back, as Aegon really wanted Harrenhal.

711
00:43:28,500 --> 00:43:30,989
But Aemond points out this war will not be one with just dragons.

712
00:43:31,619 --> 00:43:36,760
This ultimately proves that Aemond is the better strategist than Aegon, and maybe possibly the better king.

713
00:43:37,179 --> 00:43:38,079
And this upsets Aegon.

714
00:43:38,440 --> 00:43:41,239
Aegon complains to his mother about this, but Alicent comforts him,

715
00:43:41,360 --> 00:43:43,900
saying that sometimes the best a king can do is nothing.

716
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:47,400
However, Aegon grows restless with just sitting around doing nothing,

717
00:43:47,820 --> 00:43:50,320
so he decides to join the fight riding his dragon Sunfire.

718
00:43:50,820 --> 00:43:52,679
So much for not getting killed on the battlefield.

719
00:43:53,260 --> 00:43:57,059
Back at Dragonstone, Rhaenyra is informed about Kristen attacking Rook's Rest,

720
00:43:57,340 --> 00:43:59,519
and Jace suggests that they send a dragon aid their allies.

721
00:43:59,980 --> 00:44:03,380
Rhaenyra volunteers to go, so that their enemies no longer see her as weak,

722
00:44:03,659 --> 00:44:04,840
but Jace wants to go instead.

723
00:44:05,300 --> 00:44:08,639
Rhaenyra forbids it, so Rhaenys volunteers to ride out and fight with Mailees.

724
00:44:09,059 --> 00:44:11,280
Kristen attacks Rook's Rest with 1,500 men,

725
00:44:11,559 --> 00:44:12,760
and an epic battle ensues.

726
00:44:13,159 --> 00:44:17,500
Rhaenys arrives with her dragon, but Kristen prepares for this, as Aemond is already here with Vhagar.

727
00:44:17,820 --> 00:44:18,320
No, shit.

728
00:44:18,579 --> 00:44:24,079
However, Aemond holds off his attack when he sees Aegon here with his dragon, calling Aegon an idiot.

729
00:44:24,579 --> 00:44:29,199
Rhaenys engages Aegon with her bigger dragon, prompting Aemond to finally enter the battlefield.

730
00:44:29,780 --> 00:44:32,780
Aegon thanks the gods for Aemond's arrival, thinking he's here to save him,

731
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:37,519
but Aemond attacks both Rhaenys and his brother, burning Aegon and his dragon.

732
00:44:37,920 --> 00:44:41,840
Despite being outmatched against Vhagar, Rhaenys commands her dragon to attack Aemond.

733
00:44:42,099 --> 00:44:44,679
The dragons attack each other in a beautiful dance of teeth and fire,

734
00:44:45,239 --> 00:44:47,519
and Kristen is injured as Vhagar crashes to the ground.

735
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:50,639
Vhagar recovers and pulls off a surprise attack on Mailees,

736
00:44:50,820 --> 00:44:53,300
sinking his teeth into her neck as they fly higher and higher.

737
00:44:53,599 --> 00:44:55,860
Her dragon gives Rhaenys one last sad look

738
00:44:56,219 --> 00:45:02,219
before falling to her death, and thus, Rhaenys, the queen who never was, dies on the back of her dragon,

739
00:45:02,639 --> 00:45:03,940
as all Targaryens should.

740
00:45:04,639 --> 00:45:09,260
Kristen awakens to find Mailees' falling corpse had opened a hole in the castle's walls when it crash-landed,

741
00:45:09,500 --> 00:45:10,880
thus giving Kristen his forces the victory.

742
00:45:11,380 --> 00:45:14,019
He finds Aegon's crash site, but Aemond is already there.

743
00:45:14,320 --> 00:45:15,659
He looks as if he's about to kill his brother,

744
00:45:15,940 --> 00:45:20,179
but Aemond simply points at Aegon's burned body, resting beside his dead dragon, barely breathing.

745
00:45:20,780 --> 00:45:24,500
Episode 5 begins with Corlys, Rhaenyra, and Bhaela mourning the death of Rhaenys,

746
00:45:24,920 --> 00:45:29,440
and Kristen parading Mailees' head through the streets of King's Landing, declaring Aegon was the one who slew her.

747
00:45:29,820 --> 00:45:33,710
This is an awesome sight, because the common folk always believed the dragon to be totally gods.

748
00:45:34,219 --> 00:45:37,480
Then again, many of them are starving, so some of them just see the dragon at his meet.

749
00:45:38,059 --> 00:45:43,239
Aegon's burnt body is taken to his chambers, where Orwyle uses all of his maestro skills to keep him alive.

750
00:45:43,900 --> 00:45:47,460
Alicent is shattered when she sees her son is in his burnt, comatose state,

751
00:45:47,699 --> 00:45:50,500
and Aemond volunteers to rule in Aegon's place while he recovers.

752
00:45:50,920 --> 00:45:52,900
That is, if he recovers.

753
00:45:53,619 --> 00:45:56,300
Alicent then asks Kristen what happened, and why Aemond was there,

754
00:45:56,780 --> 00:45:58,559
but Kristen withholds information about what happened.

755
00:45:59,039 --> 00:46:02,739
At the next small council meeting, Alicent offers to be King Regent till Aegon recovers.

756
00:46:03,400 --> 00:46:05,199
However, the others believe Aemond would be better suited,

757
00:46:05,539 --> 00:46:08,219
because he is a dragon, and because he's a man.

758
00:46:08,599 --> 00:46:13,619
This upsets Alicent, because she believes Aemond is too reckless and impulsive, much like Daemon,

759
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:16,219
and she gets even more upset when Kristen doesn't take her side.

760
00:46:16,579 --> 00:46:20,199
Later, Aemond releases her from the council, believing she's no longer useful.

761
00:46:20,639 --> 00:46:23,880
During this time, Hugh and his family, like all the other common folk in King's Landing,

762
00:46:24,179 --> 00:46:27,119
have been starving as Aegon hasn't kept his promise to take care of them.

763
00:46:27,420 --> 00:46:30,179
They try to leave the city, but with Aemond's new orders as regent,

764
00:46:30,480 --> 00:46:33,079
they are forced to return to their homes hungry, as the city gates are closed.

765
00:46:33,679 --> 00:46:35,079
Hugh's daughter dies shortly after.

766
00:46:35,599 --> 00:46:38,119
With Rook's rest gone, and their list of allies growing thin,

767
00:46:38,519 --> 00:46:40,900
Jace realizes he can gain the support of the Freys,

768
00:46:41,260 --> 00:46:44,159
and allow Cregan's dark to cross into the Riverlands through the Twins.

769
00:46:44,579 --> 00:46:49,900
At the Twins, Jace negotiates with Lord Forest Frey for Harrenhal, in exchange for the protection of their dragons.

770
00:46:50,480 --> 00:46:53,280
Jace returns to Dragonstone to find Rhaenyra distressed,

771
00:46:53,539 --> 00:46:55,139
but she hasn't been able to do more in this war.

772
00:46:55,599 --> 00:47:00,099
Jace reminds her that they still have two dragons without any riders, Vermithor

773
00:47:00,380 --> 00:47:03,099
and Silverwing, and if they found riders for them, they would have to be a good one.

774
00:47:03,119 --> 00:47:04,059
have a better chance at winning.

775
00:47:04,500 --> 00:47:07,239
Rhaenyra reminds Jace that they don't have any more riders to spare,

776
00:47:07,539 --> 00:47:11,840
so Jace suggests finding all the Targaryen bastard children and see if they could ride the two dragons.

777
00:47:12,380 --> 00:47:13,900
It's a crazy idea.

778
00:47:14,320 --> 00:47:16,820
One could say it's a mad idea.

779
00:47:17,820 --> 00:47:23,059
Episode 6 begins with Rhaenyra and the others trying to bond Lannor's old dragon, Seasmoke, with Ser Stefan Darklyn,

780
00:47:23,559 --> 00:47:24,780
a distant Targaryen cousin.

781
00:47:25,159 --> 00:47:28,000
I know I mentioned this in the Game of Thrones video, but I mentioned it again.

782
00:47:28,179 --> 00:47:30,059
Only those with Valyrian blood can ride dragons.

783
00:47:33,119 --> 00:47:33,659
Rhaenyra generated instead.

784
00:47:34,420 --> 00:47:36,539
Guess he was too distant of a cousin.

785
00:47:37,139 --> 00:47:40,559
Aegon finally regains consciousness, but he's still very weak and covered in burns.

786
00:47:41,039 --> 00:47:44,000
Aemon speaks with him alone and asks if he remembers anything from the battle.

787
00:47:44,639 --> 00:47:47,219
Aegon says he doesn't, so Aemon makes sure he never does.

788
00:47:47,780 --> 00:47:52,059
Later, Larys sympathizes with Aegon and his injuries, as they will take a long time to heal.

789
00:47:52,380 --> 00:47:55,739
Aegon had shattered his legs so much, there's a good chance that he's never going to walk again,

790
00:47:56,059 --> 00:47:59,119
so Larys, a cripple, urges Aegon to not destroy his mind

791
00:47:59,539 --> 00:48:01,300
because that will be the only weapon that he has.

792
00:48:03,119 --> 00:48:05,280
Aemon folk to starve so he can feed his dragons and armies.

793
00:48:05,679 --> 00:48:10,260
So Rhaenyra, along with Massaria's help, decides to use this against Aemon by sending food to them,

794
00:48:10,679 --> 00:48:12,099
hoping to get them to side with her.

795
00:48:12,519 --> 00:48:17,239
Q finds out about this and quickly gets enough food for his family before Aemon's soldiers come to claim it.

796
00:48:17,559 --> 00:48:21,559
At this moment, Alicent and Helena were praying in the Grand Septa,

797
00:48:21,880 --> 00:48:24,739
so several Kingsguard quickly escort them before the crowds turn on them.

798
00:48:25,159 --> 00:48:28,960
They're too late, and things get ugly as food is thrown at them and blood is spilt.

799
00:48:29,420 --> 00:48:31,679
I'd say Rhaenyra's plan worked like a charm.

800
00:48:31,760 --> 00:48:36,739
Meanwhile, Corlys, who has now become Hand of the King, asks Alan to be his first mate aboard his ship.

801
00:48:37,139 --> 00:48:40,960
Alan is hesitant to take the position, already well aware that he's a bastard son,

802
00:48:41,260 --> 00:48:46,059
and Alan's brother, Adam, scolds Alan for not taking advantage of the luxurious life they could have had.

803
00:48:46,480 --> 00:48:48,019
Alan tells his brother to get over it.

804
00:48:48,440 --> 00:48:51,699
Later, Adam is out fishing when Seasmoke appears and starts attacking him.

805
00:48:52,000 --> 00:48:53,880
Adam runs away, but Seasmoke catches him.

806
00:48:54,079 --> 00:48:56,760
However, Seasmoke doesn't kill Adam, he just sniffs him.

807
00:48:57,099 --> 00:49:01,719
Elsewhere, Massaria and Rhaenyra rejoice in the success of their plan to turn the people against Alicent.

808
00:49:02,199 --> 00:49:03,699
They end up sharing a passionate kiss.

809
00:49:04,119 --> 00:49:08,820
They're interrupted when one of her Queensguard informs her that Adam is now riding Seasmoke.

810
00:49:09,059 --> 00:49:14,099
What? Episode 7 begins with Rhaenyra confronting Adam and wondering how he's able to ride a dragon.

811
00:49:14,559 --> 00:49:16,079
Adam claims Seasmoke chose him.

812
00:49:16,539 --> 00:49:18,980
All he wants to do is learn how to be a dragon rider and serve his queen.

813
00:49:19,380 --> 00:49:21,179
It's obvious he's also the bastard son of Corlys,

814
00:49:21,559 --> 00:49:24,739
so Rhaenyra accepts his request and has him come back with her to Dragonstone.

815
00:49:25,300 --> 00:49:27,260
He's finally getting that luxury that he always wanted.

816
00:49:27,780 --> 00:49:29,940
Upon returning, Jace confronts his mother about this,

817
00:49:30,300 --> 00:49:36,360
arguing that these new bastard dragon riders could challenge the Targaryen's power and threaten the succession due to his own illegitimate birth.

818
00:49:36,920 --> 00:49:42,260
It's blatantly obvious Harwin is his father, not Laenar, and he begs Rhaenyra to not pursue getting more riders.

819
00:49:42,719 --> 00:49:44,420
She tells Jace she doesn't have a choice,

820
00:49:44,840 --> 00:49:45,460
and he storms out.

821
00:49:45,820 --> 00:49:51,679
Massaria then uses her vast network of spies and whisperers to track down every Valyrian bastard in King's Landing in

822
00:49:51,679 --> 00:49:53,440
the hopes of getting them to become dragon riders.

823
00:49:54,019 --> 00:49:55,599
Hugh and Ulf are among them.

824
00:49:55,940 --> 00:49:56,579
Hugh wants to go.

825
00:49:56,880 --> 00:50:00,099
As his mother, a prostitute, always told him he had Valyrian blood in him.

826
00:50:00,380 --> 00:50:04,139
Ulf is hesitant, but his friends rally back his confidence, calling him a dragon lord.

827
00:50:04,400 --> 00:50:06,840
They, along with some 50 others, arrive in Dragonstone.

828
00:50:07,559 --> 00:50:11,820
Rhaenyra gives them all one last chance to turn back, as there's no guarantee any of them will survive this,

829
00:50:12,159 --> 00:50:16,059
but promises them that if they do, they will be able to bring peace and save their families back home.

830
00:50:16,320 --> 00:50:18,019
They start with trying to get a rider for Vermithor,

831
00:50:18,559 --> 00:50:20,780
but Vermithor ends up incinerating many of them.

832
00:50:21,079 --> 00:50:25,940
Amidst the panic and chaos, Hugh is miraculously able to get Vermithor to serve him after showing no fear.

833
00:50:26,039 --> 00:50:29,539
Meanwhile, Ulf was knocked down to the lower levels and tried to escape out of the way,

834
00:50:29,980 --> 00:50:31,840
accidentally coming face-to-face with Silverwing.

835
00:50:32,059 --> 00:50:35,380
However, despite showing lots of fear, Silverwing doesn't kill him,

836
00:50:35,659 --> 00:50:37,159
and Ulf becomes the second dragon rider.

837
00:50:37,599 --> 00:50:39,780
I guess, Rhaenyra got her army of bastards,

838
00:50:40,039 --> 00:50:40,440
after all.

839
00:50:40,920 --> 00:50:43,780
In the last episode of Season 2, we see that during all of this,

840
00:50:44,039 --> 00:50:46,699
Tylan has been trying to recruit the Triarchy as allies.

841
00:50:47,139 --> 00:50:49,739
The Triarchy will only join Aemond if they give back the Stepstones,

842
00:50:50,280 --> 00:50:55,679
and if Tylan can defeat their fiercest admirable, Sharaka Lahar, as the men are very loyal to him.

843
00:50:56,119 --> 00:50:57,980
Him? Sorry, I meant her.

844
00:50:58,679 --> 00:51:03,260
Tylan and Lahar engage in mud wrestling, and despite Lahar being very strong for a woman,

845
00:51:03,539 --> 00:51:05,679
Tylan manages to defeat her and gain her support.

846
00:51:06,219 --> 00:51:07,420
Amongst other things.

847
00:51:08,519 --> 00:51:10,219
I want you to f*** my wives.

848
00:51:10,800 --> 00:51:13,780
As Aegon recovers, Larys has been his most trusted ally.

849
00:51:14,300 --> 00:51:18,500
One day, he comes to Aegon, insisting that they leave King's Landing and hide out in Braavos,

850
00:51:18,840 --> 00:51:22,199
where Harrenhal's gold is stashed, and then reclaim the throne when the war is over.

851
00:51:22,739 --> 00:51:23,800
Aegon doesn't like the idea,

852
00:51:23,980 --> 00:51:30,219
until Larys fills his head with inspiring titles of what Aegon's name could be when he reclaims the throne and unites the people against Aemond.

853
00:51:30,539 --> 00:51:35,300
Upon finding out that Rhaenyra has three new dragon riders, Aemond snaps and burns everyone in Sharppoint,

854
00:51:35,780 --> 00:51:37,719
which housed a noble house loyal to Rhaenyra.

855
00:51:38,079 --> 00:51:41,619
Aemond then tries to convince the passive Helena to ride her dragon, Dreamfire,

856
00:51:42,099 --> 00:51:42,619
but she refuses.

857
00:51:43,239 --> 00:51:45,719
She then says that she knows Aemond tried to kill Aegon,

858
00:51:46,000 --> 00:51:49,239
and reveals a vision that she had of Aegon sitting on a wooden throne,

859
00:51:49,619 --> 00:51:50,420
but Aemond was dead.

860
00:51:50,619 --> 00:51:51,110
It's pretty spooky.

861
00:51:51,539 --> 00:51:54,780
Back at King's Landing, Jace finally meets the three new dragon riders,

862
00:51:55,179 --> 00:51:59,510
and becomes at odds with them, especially Ulf, when they don't take the destruction of Sharppoint seriously.

863
00:51:59,940 --> 00:52:03,280
They also don't take the sacred duty of being a dragon rider seriously at all.

864
00:52:03,860 --> 00:52:07,059
I will see you hanged, and your body fed to the dogs in the street!

865
00:52:07,519 --> 00:52:09,159
That night, Rhaenyra addresses all of them,

866
00:52:09,239 --> 00:52:12,820
telling them that they must strike Aemond's forces while they have the advantage and end the war.

867
00:52:13,139 --> 00:52:18,079
This would require killing innocents, and some of concerns regarding taking another life, let alone fighting Vhagar.

868
00:52:18,500 --> 00:52:20,940
But Jace assures them that they don't have a choice now.

869
00:52:21,519 --> 00:52:24,599
At that moment, Rhaenyra receives a message from Simon at Harrenhal.

870
00:52:24,960 --> 00:52:30,159
Daemon more or less united the Blackwoods and Brackens to serve Rhaenyra, despite his actions possibly heightening their feud.

871
00:52:30,380 --> 00:52:33,440
But now, Simon fears that Daemon may be raising the army against Rhaenyra.

872
00:52:33,900 --> 00:52:35,199
She then takes Adam with her to Harrenhal.

873
00:52:35,659 --> 00:52:38,300
Back at Harrenhal, Alice takes Daemon to a weirwood tree,

874
00:52:38,539 --> 00:52:41,980
where she shows him a vision of the White Walkers and Daenerys Targaryen.

875
00:52:42,300 --> 00:52:44,980
He learns that he has but one part to play in a vast story,

876
00:52:45,360 --> 00:52:47,480
realizing he was never actually destined to rule.

877
00:52:47,860 --> 00:52:48,320
But to serve.

878
00:52:48,760 --> 00:52:52,099
Rhaenyra and Adam arrive at Harrenhal, where she finds Daemon with his army.

879
00:52:52,440 --> 00:52:53,940
He warns her of the vision he saw,

880
00:52:54,219 --> 00:52:55,420
and that this war is just the beginning,

881
00:52:55,760 --> 00:52:57,179
because winter is coming.

882
00:52:57,579 --> 00:53:00,980
He's realized that Viserys made the right choice in naming Rhaenyra his heir,

883
00:53:01,320 --> 00:53:03,340
and bends the knee to her, along with his army.

884
00:53:03,679 --> 00:53:06,679
Rhaenyra is speechless, knowing she can outtress Daemon again.

885
00:53:07,039 --> 00:53:11,059
The repairs to Corlys' ship are completed, and Corlys tries to be a father figure to Alan.

886
00:53:11,519 --> 00:53:16,539
Alan rejects Corlys' reconciliation attempts, because he's furious that Corlys abandoned him and Adam,

887
00:53:16,960 --> 00:53:17,559
only to want to be the father figure.

888
00:53:17,579 --> 00:53:19,340
their father when his children are dead.

889
00:53:19,780 --> 00:53:24,219
Rhaenyra returns to Dragonstone, and that night she gets an unexpected visitor, Alicent.

890
00:53:24,800 --> 00:53:27,219
Alicent has had enough of this endless plotting and striving,

891
00:53:27,480 --> 00:53:31,079
and wishes to surrender King's Landing to her, in exchange for her and her family's safety.

892
00:53:31,559 --> 00:53:35,019
Rhaenyra doesn't believe what she's hearing, but Alicent knows Rhaenyra will win this war,

893
00:53:35,219 --> 00:53:37,079
admitting that there has already been enough bloodshed.

894
00:53:37,739 --> 00:53:41,599
But Rhaenyra doesn't think so, and only agrees to Alicent's terms if Aegon is killed.

895
00:53:42,199 --> 00:53:45,920
The choice is hard for Alicent, but she silently acknowledges that there's no other option.

896
00:53:46,320 --> 00:53:49,199
She tells Rhaenyra that the gates to King's Landing will open in three days,

897
00:53:49,579 --> 00:53:51,340
allowing Rhaenyra to take the city as she pleases.

898
00:53:51,780 --> 00:53:55,840
The season ends with a montage of countless people and armies preparing for battle all across Westeros.

899
00:53:56,360 --> 00:53:58,519
We get a glimpse of Otto locked away in a cell somewhere,

900
00:53:58,780 --> 00:54:00,760
while Larrus and Aegon nick their way to Braavos.

901
00:54:01,360 --> 00:54:03,380
Who will win the great war that is to come?

902
00:54:03,840 --> 00:54:06,079
We'll have to wait until the summer of 2026.

903
00:54:07,449 --> 00:54:09,900
I hate when a show ends on a cliffhanger.

904
00:54:10,139 --> 00:54:11,420
I can't wait to find out what happens next.

905
00:54:11,800 --> 00:54:14,480
But in the meantime, I guess you could watch the new Game of Thrones prequel show,

906
00:54:14,599 --> 00:54:16,570
A Night of the Seven Kingdoms, coming out in January.

907
00:54:16,920 --> 00:54:20,440
Anyway, feel free to click on the video on screen to watch another one of our videos.

908
00:54:20,820 --> 00:54:21,699
We'll see you next time.

909
00:54:22,119 --> 00:54:22,380
See ya!

